The rest of the package was written for BootLoops, in part as an
implementation of the equations of the two papers: the parser, the counting
algorithm of src/staircase.jl, the minimal-polynomial candidate routes, the
rational reconstruction, the command-line program and the tests. PATCHES.md
beside this file gives the full account, with line counts.

The article text of arXiv:2606.29612 is under CC BY 4.0. Test expectations:
the sunrise is the worked example of that paper; the equal-mass bubble is the
Type-1.2 example of the authors' demo notebook (functions_demo.nb in
Landau-s-Leviathans). No data file of the authors is redistributed here.

OSCAR, which this package calls at run time, is GPL-3.0-or-later and is
installed through the Julia package manager; it is not bundled.
